cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the DSI laboratory, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DSI Laboratory: Dynamics of Invariants for the b-C/a-C Framework"
authors:
  - family-names: "Isaev"
    given-names: "Ishak Khamzatovich"
    email: "aslan08_05@mail.ru"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7299-0701"
date-released: 2026-10-12
version: "2.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wild8highlander/choptuik_ac_bc"
abstract: >
  A self-contained package of seven deterministic experiments on the open
  problems of the b-C/a-C spinor-correction framework: the sharp trace
  theorem and the partial-isometry theorems A/B/C (Kunz defect), the
  census attack on DSI-4 (9/224 via the {7,3} tiling of the Klein quartic),
  the Hurwitz-tower audit with correction D1 (PSL(2,13)), the falsifiable
  QNM overtone law, and the QCD-bridge centering correction E1. Includes
  a Lean 4 formalization of the exact theorem stratum, a six-language
  cross-verification core, bilingual monographs, animations, and a
  committed claim ledger with honesty statuses.
keywords:
  - "Klein quartic"
  - "PSL(2,7)"
  - "Cuntz algebra"
  - "partial isometries"
  - "Choptuik"
  - "continued fractions"
  - "Hurwitz tower"
  - "Lean 4"
license-url: "https://github.com/wild8highlander/choptuik_ac_bc/blob/main/LICENSE"
